{"id":"1e9aa7b3ae40ed8b","group":"27","path":"27/27-thm-clausetautology.md","title":"Tautological raw clauses and clause normalization","display":"thm-clausetautology — Tautological raw clauses and clause normalization","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications","book_abbrev":"27","label":"27-thm-clausetautology","aliases":["27-thm-clausetautology"],"display":"thm-clausetautology — Tautological raw clauses and clause normalization","depends_on":["[[27-df-literal]]","[[27-df-constfunc]]"],"source_file":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf","source_section":"§1.2 Boolean identities; §1.4 Definition 1.10","source_printed_pages":"9, 15","source_pdf_pages":"33, 39","verification_status":"proved-in-note-from-source-definitions","local_revision_status":"formal-audit-2026-10-20; source-not-rechecked"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"27"},{"key":"label","html":"27-thm-clausetautology"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>27-thm-clausetautology</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-clausetautology — Tautological raw clauses and clause normalization"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"99c92f3457aacd12\" href=\"?note=99c92f3457aacd12\" title=\"27-df-literal\">27-df-literal</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"35eab4f22873ea23\" href=\"?note=35eab4f22873ea23\" title=\"27-df-constfunc\">27-df-constfunc</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_file","html":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf"},{"key":"source_section","html":"§1.2 Boolean identities; §1.4 Definition 1.10"},{"key":"source_printed_pages","html":"9, 15"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"33, 39"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"proved-in-note-from-source-definitions"},{"key":"local_revision_status","html":"formal-audit-2026-10-20; source-not-rechecked"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(n\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\subseteq\\mathrm{Lit}_n\">\\(L\\subseteq\\mathrm{Lit}_n\\)</span> 是任意文字集；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Lit}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{Lit}_n\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"99c92f3457aacd12\" href=\"?note=99c92f3457aacd12\" title=\"27-df-literal\">27-df-literal</a>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbf1_n\">\\(\\mathbf1_n\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"35eab4f22873ea23\" href=\"?note=35eab4f22873ea23\" title=\"27-df-constfunc\">27-df-constfunc</a>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"C^*_L\\coloneqq\\left\\{\\left(a,1-\\prod_{\\ell\\in L}(1-\\ell(a))\\right)\\mid a\\in\\mathbb B^n\\right\\},\\qquad\\prod_{\\ell\\in\\emptyset}(1-\\ell(a))\\coloneqq1.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[C^*_L\\coloneqq\\left\\{\\left(a,1-\\prod_{\\ell\\in L}(1-\\ell(a))\\right)\\mid a\\in\\mathbb B^n\\right\\},\\qquad\\prod_{\\ell\\in\\emptyset}(1-\\ell(a))\\coloneqq1.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"C^*_L=\\mathbf1_n\\quad\\leftrightarrow\\quad\\exists i\\in[n]\\;(\\{x_i,\\bar x_i\\}\\subseteq L).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[C^*_L=\\mathbf1_n\\quad\\leftrightarrow\\quad\\exists i\\in[n]\\;(\\{x_i,\\bar x_i\\}\\subseteq L).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>含互补对的原始析取恒真；若无互补对，则可同时令所有文字为 0，故不恒真。Clause_n 本身按 Definition 1.10 已排除此类原始恒真析取，本定理在任意文字集上解释标准化步骤，不能误作整个 CNF 的 satisfiability 判据。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"27-df-literal","status":"resolved","id":"99c92f3457aacd12","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-literal]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-constfunc","status":"resolved","id":"35eab4f22873ea23","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-constfunc]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-literal","status":"resolved","id":"99c92f3457aacd12","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$n\\in\\mathbb N$，$L\\subseteq\\mathrm{Lit}_n$ 是任意文字集；$\\mathrm{Lit}_n$ 见 [[27-df-literal]]，$\\mathbf1_n$ 见 [[27-df-constfunc]]。","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-constfunc","status":"resolved","id":"35eab4f22873ea23","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$n\\in\\mathbb N$，$L\\subseteq\\mathrm{Lit}_n$ 是任意文字集；$\\mathrm{Lit}_n$ 见 [[27-df-literal]]，$\\mathbf1_n$ 见 [[27-df-constfunc]]。","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\mathbb N","display":false},{"tex":"L\\subseteq\\mathrm{Lit}_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Lit}_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbf1_n","display":false},{"tex":"C^*_L\\coloneqq\\left\\{\\left(a,1-\\prod_{\\ell\\in L}(1-\\ell(a))\\right)\\mid a\\in\\mathbb B^n\\right\\},\\qquad\\prod_{\\ell\\in\\emptyset}(1-\\ell(a))\\coloneqq1.","display":true},{"tex":"C^*_L=\\mathbf1_n\\quad\\leftrightarrow\\quad\\exists i\\in[n]\\;(\\{x_i,\\bar x_i\\}\\subseteq L).","display":true}],"bytes":1577,"backlinks":[{"id":"5244dbb38da17b8a","anchor":"ref-388","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[27-thm-clausetautology|thm-clausetautology — Tautological raw clauses and clause normalization]]"}],"outgoing":["99c92f3457aacd12","35eab4f22873ea23"]}